// The dagger.v1 services: three faces over one contract. GraphService reads
// and mutates the graph, WorkService hands out and manages leases, and
// EventService serves the change stream. docs/domain-model.md is the
// rationale; docs/architecture.md says where each is served.
//
// Node references. Wherever a request names a node it does so with a single
// string in one of four forms: "#7" for a node in the request's project,
// "slug#7" for a node in another project of the same organization,
// "org/slug#7" fully qualified, or an alias declared by a create_node
// operation earlier in the same patch. The server never asks a client for a
// node id, and resolution returns the node's title so a caller can check
// that a dense number resolved to the node it meant.
//
// Idempotency. Every RPC that writes carries a client-supplied request_id.
// A repeated request_id returns the original result; the same id with
// different content is an error rather than a silent replay.
//
// Provenance is never client-assertable. Requests carry no principal; the
// server resolves the actor from the transport. See
